        "comments": "Source DNA is available from State Key Laboratory of Pathogen and Biosecurity, Beijing Institute of Microbiology and Epidemiology, Beijing, 100071, P. R. China. Bacteria available from ATCC (ATCC 33279).\nSource DNA is available from State Key Laboratory of Pathogen and Biosecurity, Beijing Institute of Microbiology and Epidemiology, Beijing, 100071, P. R. China. Bacteria available from ATCC (ATCC 33279).\nThe chromosome sequence was aligned to the Legionella pneumophila Paris reference genome in NC_006368. A single contig was split into two, AGVU01000025 and AGVU01000001, in order to make dnaA the first gene in the chromosome. Consequently, the first and last contigs are contiguous.\npLDNY1 plasmid sequence was aligned to pLD-TEX-KL plasmid sequence of Fluoribacter dumoffii TEX-KL in AB297474.\npLDNY2 plasmid sequence was aligned to pLPP plasmid sequence of Legionella pneumophila Paris in NC_006365.\nThe annotation was added by the NCBI Prokaryotic Genome Annotation Pipeline (PGAP). Information about PGAP can be found here: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genome/annotation_prok/",
